    "introduction": "Haleon develops and markets consumer-healthcare products that people can often buy without a prescription. Its portfolio includes oral-care, pain-relief, digestive-health and vitamin products, with brands such as Sensodyne, Panadol, Advil and Centrum. Products reach consumers through pharmacies, supermarkets, other retailers and online channels. Revenue depends on repeat purchases, brand recognition and the perceived effectiveness of its products. The business combines scientific formulation, marketing and manufacturing, with professional recommendations relevant in areas such as oral health. Consumer spending and seasonal illness can affect demand, while product regulation, quality control and ingredient or packaging costs influence operations across its international markets.",
